From 77f933cd8a7ce9db5bacaf1e92ecfa09c962589e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duckfamily <156525766+duckfamily@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:33:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Add custom wallpapers behind the chat and chat list

One cover-scaled frame painted in top-level-window coordinates, so the two
columns form a single continuous surface.

Animated files are decoded with FFmpeg::FrameGenerator, not
Media::Clip::Reader. The clip reader caps decoding at 1280x720 and sets that
as max_pixels before avcodec_open2, so any ordinary 1080p file made the codec
refuse to open with EINVAL and no frame ever appeared. That limit is right
for inline previews inside a chat and wrong for a full-screen wallpaper.

The clip reader could not report the failure either: Manager
handleProcessResult posts the error notification to the main thread and then
erases the reader from its own map before that post runs, so the carries()
check drops it. A file that cannot be opened looks exactly like one that was
never processed.

Frames are decoded at the window's own size and blitted without a transform.
Scaling them down on every paint, from both the chat list and the chat, was
what made an animated wallpaper stutter; this also removes a second
resampling pass, so the picture is sharper as well as cheaper.

Every failure path logs. The feature originally had no diagnostics at all,
which is why nobody could tell the decoder was rejecting the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
